00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:08.281
There were plenty of popular theories before
Black Panther was released that the movie

00:01:08.281 --> 00:01:10.520
would reveal the Soul Stone was in Wakanda.

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:13.700
If you've seen the film, you'll know that
didn't happen, however, there's still a chance

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:16.790
that the Stone is hidden somewhere in the
African nation.

00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:20.950
We know from Black Panther's prologue that
Wakanda's vibranium came from a meteorite

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:23.510
that hit the earth and then affected the plant
life.

00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:27.090
There's quite a convincing theory that the
Soul Stone is buried deep in the centre of

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:31.860
the meteorite and it's that Infinity Stone
which gives the Heart-Shaped Herb its extraordinary

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:32.860
properties.

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:36.590
This Soul Stone theory could also explain
why the plant gives the person who ingests

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:40.940
it access to the ancestral plane and the ability
to communicate with the souls of the dead.

00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:46.560
By the way, the Soul Stone endowing the Heart-Shaped
Herb with its powers would also fit the THANOS

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:50.790
theory, and I'll explain what that means later
for those who don't already know.

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:54.560
One potential problem with this theory is
that the Soul Stone is orange-coloured, whereas

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:56.120
the Heart-Shaped Herb is purple.

00:01:56.120 --> 00:02:00.570
However, the colours of the Infinity Stones
and the powers they grant do not always have

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:01.789
to match.

00:02:01.789 --> 00:02:06.920
Scarlet Witch derives her power from the yellow
Mind Stone, but her powers are red.

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:11.970
Also when we first encounter the Mind Stone
in Loki's sceptre, it looks blue, but later

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:15.790
when it's broken open, the Stone's true yellow
colour is revealed.

00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:20.170
There is a potential wrinkle in this theory,
though, which is that Black Panther director

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:23.721
Ryan Coogler has specifically said about the
Soul Stone that

00:02:23.721 --> 00:02:27.830
"I love the Infinity Stones as much as any
comic book fan, it's just Wakanda already

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:29.710
has its thing, which is Vibranium.

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:34.800
For us, that was special enough, so to throw
in something like another special thing didn't

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:36.050
feel right.

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:40.870
It felt like we should stick with our one
MacGuffin for the country and explore that.

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:45.490
[Marvel Studios] never really was interested
in putting a stone in there, either."

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:50.490
Now, that makes total sense as the movie gave
us an awesome introduction to Wakanda and

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:55.240
it had a lot to pack into its runtime, so
if they'd had to also include and explain

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:59.870
the Soul Stone, it might have all felt like
a bit too much and taken the shine away from

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:03.660
the main story just in order to set up a future
story.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:08.500
But let's remember that Coogler is only talking
about his own Black Panther solo movie and,

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:12.580
so, Marvel might still choose to reveal that
the Soul Stone is in Wakanda in their next

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:14.660
film, Avengers: Infinity War.

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:18.440
Ok, let's get into the Infinity Stone theories
for that movie.

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:23.070
We've seen quite a bit of footage of Thanos
sending a huge army of Outriders to invade

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:28.060
Wakanda, and because we know he's trying to
complete his Infinity Gauntlet, it seems highly

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:30.570
possible that he's after an Infinity Stone.

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:35.550
Among a range of Infinity War Lego sets are
two different Infinity Stone scenes set in

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:36.550
Wakanda.

00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:41.890
In one set, you can see one of Thanos's Black
Order, Proxima Midnight, trying to steal an

00:03:41.890 --> 00:03:43.550
orangey-looking Stone.

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:48.270
A leaked description for the Lego set also
specifically says that Falcon is diving down

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:50.250
to save the Soul Stone.

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:54.330
While in another Lego set, we can clearly
see Captain America and Black Widow defending

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:57.030
a blue Infinity Stone against an Outrider.

00:03:57.030 --> 00:04:01.620
Now, you have to bear in mind that these are
toy sets so they may be actual scenes or fairly

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:06.310
close to actual scenes, or the toy designers
may have just mixed up different elements

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:09.230
from the movie to create an enticing product
to sell.

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:13.650
I do think we'll probably get at least one
Infinity Stone turning up in Wakanda in Infinity

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:18.040
War, however, it might just be the Mind Stone,
because we know from the trailer that the

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:23.150
Black Order attempt to extract that from Vision's
forehead, so the Avengers may take him to

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:26.150
Wakanda for treatment so it can be removed
without killing him.

00:04:26.150 --> 00:04:31.230
We also know from the Avengers: Infinity War
prelude comic and the Black Panther post-credits

00:04:31.230 --> 00:04:36.130
scene that Shuri has developed tech in Wakanda
that removed the HYDRA programming from Bucky's

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:40.030
brain, and I think she may find a way to treat
Vision as well.

00:04:40.030 --> 00:04:44.730
However, we can't ignore that Thanos may simply
be invading Wakanda for access to all that

00:04:44.730 --> 00:04:49.170
precious vibranium and tech which T'Challa
was about to announce to the world in the

00:04:49.170 --> 00:04:51.370
first Black Panther end-credits scene.

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:56.170
Another alternate location for the Soul Stone
in Infinity War is the red planet Nidavellir.

00:04:56.170 --> 00:05:01.040
This planet, which is inhabited by dwarves,
is where Mjolnir was originally forged, and

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:05.990
in Infinity War, it looks like Thor travels
there with the Guardians to create a new weapon.

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:09.990
There's actually a Lego set of a scene from
the planet and it shows an Infinity Stone

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:12.590
being used for what it calls a "space forge".

00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:17.710
It's from the scene in the trailer where we
briefly see Thor straining to control a machine.

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:21.830
This Infinity Stone might or might not be
the Soul Stone, but I think it's interesting

00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:27.920
that Thor's hammer Mjolnir was, to quote Odin,
forged "in the heart of a dying star".

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:32.100
And if that "heart" of a dying star is the
location of the Soul Stone, this would also

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:34.220
fit the THANOS theory.

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:39.610
OK, before we get too attached to the idea
that the Soul Stone must be in either Wakanda

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:43.620
or somewhere else in Avengers: Infinity War,
let's look at some theories that Marvel could

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:47.400
be saving the Soul Stone for use in a film
after Infinity War.

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:52.470
The next film after Avengers: Infinity War
is Ant-Man And The Wasp and what we know so

00:05:52.470 --> 00:05:55.130
far is that the movie will travel to the Quantum
Realm.

00:05:55.130 --> 00:06:00.150
We haven't seen very much of the Quantum Realm
yet in the MCU with just glimpses in Doctor

00:06:00.150 --> 00:06:02.130
Strange and the first Ant-Man movie.

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:06.840
So, if Marvel felt they wanted the story and
box-office pay-off from the reveal of a new

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:11.639
Infinity Stone in Ant-Man And The Wasp rather
than Avengers: Infinity War, the Quantum Realm

00:06:11.639 --> 00:06:16.100
would be a good place to explain where the
Soul Stone's been all these years.

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:19.340
And there's actually a precedent in the comics
for the Soul Stone/an Infinity Stone existing

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:21.270
at the subatomic level.

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:26.430
In a 1980s Incredible Hulk storyline, Bruce
Banner travelled to the subatomic world of

00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:30.010
K'ai where he encountered an Elder of the
Universe called the Gardener.

00:06:30.010 --> 00:06:34.240
At that time, the Gardener was in possession
of the an Infinity Gem and had travelled to

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:37.460
K'ai in order to keep the power of the gem
away from humanity.

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:41.660
I certainly wouldn't expect this story to
play out exactly like this in Ant-Man And

00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:46.610
The Wasp, however, Scott Lang and Hope van
Dyne could encounter a new Elder of the Universe

00:06:46.610 --> 00:06:49.690
who controls or has access to the Soul Stone.

00:06:49.690 --> 00:06:53.490
After all, the Elders of the Universe have
already been introduced in the MCU in the

00:06:53.490 --> 00:06:55.420
form of the Collector and the Grandmaster.

00:06:55.420 --> 00:07:00.810
And it looks like the Quantum Realm will play
a crucial role in linking all the movies between

00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:05.800
Infinity War and Avengers 4 because the subatomic
world that Ant-Man And The Wasp explores will

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:11.220
also connect specifically to the Captain Marvel
movie and the rest of the MCU.

00:07:11.220 --> 00:07:16.120
Quantum physicist Dr Spiros Michalakis, who
worked as a consultant on Ant-Man, has confirmed

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:20.390
this link between the movies and has also
suggested that once superheroes like Ant-Man

00:07:20.390 --> 00:07:24.889
and the Wasp, and perhaps Captain Marvel,
begin to understand quantum code, they will

00:07:24.889 --> 00:07:28.640
be able to access powers that are considered
impossible in the normal world.

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:33.010
For instance, they could, in theory, manipulate
the physical laws of the universe like space

00:07:33.010 --> 00:07:36.290
and time to create things like black holes.

00:07:36.290 --> 00:07:40.300
And such powers would be clearly very useful
if you're up against the likes of Thanos,

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:44.520
but it really makes me wonder whether the
Soul Stone could be connected to these potential

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:46.710
new powers and abilities?

00:07:46.710 --> 00:07:51.900
And finally we come to the mother of all MCU
movies, the epic finale to everything that

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:55.360
Marvel Studios has been building to, Avengers
4.

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:58.740
So, will we have to wait till then to see
the Soul Stone?

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:03.520
Well, we know from various set photos that
it looks like the movie will incorporate time

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:04.520
travel.

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:08.150
And that ties back nicely to why the movies
Ant-Man And The Wasp and Captain Marvel have

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:13.030
been placed between Infinity War and Avengers
4 as the exploration of the Quantum Realm

00:08:13.030 --> 00:08:17.390
in those two films could open up the ability
for other Avengers beyond Doctor Strange to

00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:22.220
mess with the timeline and potentially prevent
Thanos attaining supremacy.

00:08:22.220 --> 00:08:26.389
And it's possible that Avengers 4 could be
an attempt by the Avengers to recover the

00:08:26.389 --> 00:08:29.220
Soul Stone before Thanos gets to it first.

00:08:29.220 --> 00:08:33.500
Ok, I can't finish without mentioning that
it's still possible the Soul Stone has been

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:36.870
hiding in plain sight ever since the first
Thor movie.

00:08:36.870 --> 00:08:41.820
In other words, it's located in the middle
of Heimdall's armour or even in his eyes,

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:46.110
which is one possible reason for his glowing
orange eyes and the fact that he can see trillions

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:47.580
of souls.

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:51.670
Heimdall having the Soul Stone also ties in
nicely with the T.H.A.N.O.S theory I mentioned

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:56.130
earlier that all the objects holding the Infinity
Stones in the MCU will eventually spell out

00:08:56.130 --> 00:08:57.770
the word THANOS.

00:08:57.770 --> 00:09:02.360
So far we've had the Tesseract, a 'T' for
the Space Stone; the Aether, an 'A' for the

00:09:02.360 --> 00:09:07.600
Reality Stone; Doctor Strange's Eye of Agamotto
is held on a necklace, giving an 'N' for the

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:13.240
Time Stone; the Orb which contains the Power
Stone provides an 'O'; and Loki's Sceptre

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:15.670
which held the Mind Stone, gives us an 'S'.

00:09:15.670 --> 00:09:20.690
So, Heimdall, Heart-Shaped Herb or heart of
a dying star would all provide the missing

00:09:20.690 --> 00:09:22.880
'H' for the T.H.A.N.O.S theory.

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:27.290
If the Soul Stone were in Heimdall, then Thanos
could take it when he attacks the Asgardian

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:29.580
ship after Thor: Ragnarok.

00:09:29.580 --> 00:09:34.060
And if Thanos had to kill Heimdall to get
the stone, that might lead to Loki offering

00:09:34.060 --> 00:09:37.180
Thanos the Tesseract in order to spare the
rest of the Asgardians.

